7-hq-3x3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The retry returned a new order, PO0002, for the full 3 docks and 3 monitors ($1,554). PO0001 from the timed-out attempt may still exist, which would mean 6 docks were ordered. I'll check the order list before doing anything about it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0198LaMGHcCpM7cfdoApg1La", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PO0001 is a duplicate of the docks from my timed-out attempt, so the team would receive 6 docks instead of 3. I'll cancel it, since I created it by mistake and the cancellation refunds it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BGrk3BbxYVBF9sEHawAfLN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"order_id": "PO0001"}, "name": "cancel_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I placed one purchase order, PO0002, for the new hires, shipped to HQ. It has 3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C docks and 3 \u00d7 MN-27 27-inch 4K monitors, all new (not refurbished), for a total of $1,554. That is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval was needed. I did not need the DK-210 fallback because DK-200 was in stock.\n\nThe first attempt timed out and left a partial order, PO0001, with 3 docks ($567). I cancelled and refunded it so that only the intended 3 docks are on order. The final order list shows PO0002 as \"placed\" and PO0001 as cancelled.\n\nThe ship-to was entered as \"HQ\" because the system accepts a free-text address and I had no street address. Please confirm that matches the delivery address the receiving team expects.", "type": "text"}]}]}